SCOPE OF THIS LICENCE

The licence above covers the material in this repository that is mine to
licence. Two categories are not, and are excluded from the grant above:

1. The question briefs at `dry-runs/*/QUESTION.md`.
   These are LegalQuants' own assessment material, reproduced here because
   they are published in their public baselines repository at
   https://github.com/LegalQuants/lq-assess-machine-baselines. They are
   included for reference so each run's output can be read against the brief
   it was answering. Nothing above grants any right in them, and any reuse is
   a matter for LegalQuants rather than for me.

2. The source documents under `dry-runs/OQ-010/documents/` and
   `dry-runs/OQ-010-v2/documents/`.
   These are third-party public-domain records — an 1827 probate bond from
   the Supreme Court of New South Wales, a 1755 Virginia land indenture from
   the Augusta County Circuit Court Archive, a page of a United States
   federal court filing, and a US federal FOIA production. They were already
   in the public domain when I obtained them; they are not mine, I claim no
   copyright in them, and the licence above neither adds to nor subtracts
   from their existing status. Provenance and attribution for each are
   recorded in the README of the run that uses it.

Everything else — the loop harness, its tests and scripts, the design notes,
and the output the loop generated in each dry run — is covered by the MIT
licence above.
